Feature: Resync
  A `resync` hands the editor a fresh copy of its value after `ready`. The
  copy replaces the value and clears undo history.

  Scenario Outline: Resyncing a changed word in <position> block at <depth>
    Given the editor state is "<state>"
    When the editor is resynced to "<resynced>"
    Then the editor state is "<expected>"
    When undo is performed
    Then the editor state is "<expected>"

    Examples:
